⍝ ZZ65_Regression.tc
⍝ ══════════════════

⍝@ test3.

      ⍝ bug-apl@gnu.org, Bugs8 #1 (Blake McBride):
      ⍝ IndexExpr::erase_stale() deleted *live* IndexExprs (no ownership
      ⍝ tracking at all), which is why re-enabling IndexExpr ring membership
      ⍝ (so that )CHECK's "no stale indices" diagnostic would do something)
      ⍝ was tried and reverted twice (SVN 2053/2054): a partial index left
      ⍝ on a suspended SI's prefix stack after an error got deleted early by
      ⍝ erase_stale(), then deleted *again* by Prefix::clean_up() at the
      ⍝ next )SIC/)CLEAR/)RESET -- a double free, SIGSEGV in ~IndexExpr().
      ⍝
      ⍝ Fixed by giving IndexExpr the same independent mark/unmark
      ⍝ reachability check that Value already has (Prefix::unmark_all_values()
      ⍝ now also unmarks IndexExprs reachable from TOK_PINDEX/TOK_INDEX
      ⍝ tokens, including Prefix::saved_MISC). IndexExpr::erase_stale() is
      ⍝ gone -- actual freeing stays exactly where it already correctly
      ⍝ happened; the ring/mark/unmark mechanism only ever reports, never
      ⍝ deletes, exactly like Value's.
      ⍝
      ⍝ Below: leave a partial index (the ']' already reduced, on the
      ⍝ prefix stack as a TOK_PINDEX) on a suspended SI by raising an
      ⍝ error while it is there. )CHECK while still suspended must NOT
      ⍝ report it stale (it is genuinely live); )SIC then frees it via
      ⍝ the normal path, and a second )CHECK must still report nothing.

      )CLEAR
CLEAR WS
      A←1 2 3
      A[UNDEF]
VALUE ERROR+
      A[UNDEF]
        ^
      )CHECK
OK      - no stale functions
OK      - no stale values
OK      - no stale indices
OK      - no duplicate parents
      )SIC
      )CHECK
OK      - no stale functions
OK      - no stale values
OK      - no stale indices
OK      - no duplicate parents

      ]NEXTFILE
